WEBVTT

00:01.250 --> 00:04.250
I had a lot of fun today too.

00:04.830 --> 00:08.750
So I want to hang out with you again.

00:11.080 --> 00:12.830
If you wanna.

00:12.830 --> 00:13.500
Really?

00:14.460 --> 00:15.580
It's a promise, okay?

00:21.080 --> 00:24.460
Akanesasu kousha no kage

00:24.460 --> 00:30.750
Mitsukaranai hazu no seishun no hashikko ni

00:31.000 --> 00:36.170
Sukoshi suwareta kamo, kedo sugu kiechau kamo

00:36.170 --> 00:40.420
Kimi ga waraikakete kureru koto mo

00:40.420 --> 00:42.330
Kirei da ne

00:42.330 --> 00:45.130
Kiseki tte yonde ii kana

00:45.380 --> 00:51.040
Konna hibi ga suki da yo, suki da yo, sukida yo

00:51.040 --> 00:57.500
Datte zutto tsuzuku wake janai kara, dakishimeru no

00:57.500 --> 01:01.630
Kodomo kara chotto fumidashita haru no hi ni

01:01.630 --> 01:05.040
Susume, susume, susume, ippo zutsu

01:05.040 --> 01:08.380
Ima kasuka de tashikana kaze ga fuku

01:08.380 --> 01:16.040
Semete boku to kimi no aida wa sekai ga sukoshi irozukimasu youni

01:16.040 --> 01:20.670
Donna canvas o egaku kana, donna mirai ni naru kana

01:20.670 --> 01:24.460
Wakaranai kedo shinjite mitaina

01:23.750 --> 01:28.000
Egao de te o futtara kitto

01:24.830 --> 01:27.830
Jaa mata ne to ie tara

01:27.830 --> 01:31.540
Ashita ga sukoshi tanoshimi ni naru ne

01:31.630 --> 01:38.500
Kisetsu no hayasa ni sotte, kotoba kasaneru bokura

01:38.500 --> 01:44.960
Douka douka shiawase de arimasu youni da ne

01:54.750 --> 01:59.330
<b>Episode 12: Starring Role and Gift</b>

02:01.420 --> 02:03.420
This morning is just like every other morning.

02:05.130 --> 02:07.130
There's nothing different about today.

02:08.460 --> 02:09.540
That being said...

02:11.670 --> 02:13.540
Good morning, Shiraishi-kun.

02:15.790 --> 02:16.790
Good morning,

02:17.460 --> 02:18.380
Kubo-san.

02:20.630 --> 02:22.500
Why is Kubo-san...?

02:27.290 --> 02:28.880
Hey, Shiraishi-kun.

02:30.460 --> 02:33.290
Do you believe in stuff like horoscopes
and psychological tests?

02:33.790 --> 02:35.080
That came out of nowhere.

02:35.380 --> 02:39.790
Yeah, there were psychological tests
on TV yesterday. It was interesting.

02:39.790 --> 02:41.210
Did you watch it?

02:41.580 --> 02:46.290
I didn't. I think stuff like that should
be taken with a grain of salt.

02:46.580 --> 02:47.580
What about you?

02:47.580 --> 02:49.920
I'm pretty into them.

02:50.920 --> 02:51.580
Oh!

02:52.130 --> 02:56.710
Since you didn't catch it on TV yesterday,
how about I give you a psychological test real quick?

02:57.420 --> 02:59.330
She's grinning.

02:59.330 --> 03:01.580
He-he!

03:02.750 --> 03:05.920
You're shouting in a dream.

03:06.250 --> 03:07.920
What are you shouting?

03:08.460 --> 03:09.750
Hmm.

03:10.460 --> 03:12.250
What situation would cause me to shout?

03:12.580 --> 03:15.080
Horror and whatnot doesn't bother me.

03:15.080 --> 03:17.670
I don't make a sound when I get startled.

03:18.420 --> 03:20.170
If I were to shout...

03:20.170 --> 03:20.880
Ah!

03:21.670 --> 03:24.880
Maybe "yodel-ay-hee-hoo." Like I'm on a mountain.

03:25.880 --> 03:26.960
So your answer...

03:28.420 --> 03:32.290
Is the first thing you'll shout when
you're in an extreme situation.

03:32.290 --> 03:34.000
Yodel-ay-hee-hoo!

03:34.000 --> 03:37.630
Shiraishi-kun, if you were attacked by a bear,

03:38.040 --> 03:39.960
Roar!

03:39.960 --> 03:42.920
would you shout, "Yodel-ay-hee-hoo!" as you run away?

03:42.920 --> 03:44.540
Yodel-ay-hee-hoo!

03:46.630 --> 03:48.420
Kubo-san, you're laughing too much.

03:49.460 --> 03:51.830
Sorry. Let's continue the test.

03:51.830 --> 03:53.540
Oh, there's more.

03:54.250 --> 03:56.830
You can see flowers blooming.

03:57.290 --> 03:58.880
How many flowers are blooming?

03:59.670 --> 04:00.540
How many?

04:00.830 --> 04:01.460
Yep.

04:01.460 --> 04:02.710
Answer whatever comes to mind first.

04:03.920 --> 04:04.920
Flowers...

04:07.380 --> 04:08.330
One flower.

04:11.330 --> 04:12.170
Really?

04:12.170 --> 04:14.290
Huh? What does my answer mean?

04:15.830 --> 04:16.960
Your answer is

04:18.750 --> 04:22.500
the number of people you'll date during your lifetime.

04:24.790 --> 04:25.790
Really?

04:27.670 --> 04:32.170
I don't know if I should be happy I'll get to date someone,

04:32.630 --> 04:36.830
or upset that if I let that person get away,
that'll be my last romantic relationship.

04:37.380 --> 04:38.460
I've got mixed feelings.

04:42.750 --> 04:45.960
Oh, let's try answering a psychological test together.

04:43.040 --> 04:43.710
Oh?

04:46.170 --> 04:48.920
Shiraishi-kun, look one up and ask away!

04:49.420 --> 04:50.170
Uh...

04:50.170 --> 04:51.880
A psychological test?

04:52.210 --> 04:59.210
<b>(Psychological Test) Easy!!</b>

04:52.210 --> 04:59.210
<b>Psych test: animal edition</b>

04:52.460 --> 04:54.920
We're doing it together,
so don't look at what the answer means.

04:55.080 --> 04:56.630
Okay, got it.

04:57.080 --> 04:59.210
Oh, this one should be a breeze.

04:59.460 --> 05:02.170
Um, there are kittens in your room.

05:02.170 --> 05:03.960
How many kittens are playing?

05:04.460 --> 05:05.750
What's your answer?

05:06.790 --> 05:08.500
I guess two.

05:08.920 --> 05:10.460
And I'll answer...

05:14.170 --> 05:16.330
There are oodles of kittens!

05:17.880 --> 05:19.080
Oodles?

05:19.210 --> 05:22.170
Because it's cuter when there are more!

05:22.750 --> 05:24.420
You make a compelling case.

05:24.540 --> 05:25.380
Yeah!

05:26.080 --> 05:28.250
So? What do our answers mean?

05:28.250 --> 05:29.420
Um...

05:34.380 --> 05:40.380
<b>The number of children you want to have</b>

05:47.830 --> 05:50.880
What? That was the point of the psychological test?

05:51.540 --> 05:55.880
But your answers to psychological tests can change
depending on when you take them.

05:57.330 --> 05:59.130
Y-yeah, good point.

05:59.710 --> 06:03.380
Oh! I have to get home early today, come to think of it.

06:03.380 --> 06:04.420
Oh, okay.

06:04.420 --> 06:06.630
Yep! So I'll leave first.

06:06.830 --> 06:07.710
All right.

06:07.710 --> 06:08.880
Bye, bye!

06:16.210 --> 06:17.540
I'll head home too.

06:39.830 --> 06:41.130
How shameless.

06:49.080 --> 06:51.000
Akina, you're gonna have coffee?

06:51.000 --> 06:52.460
Yep, sure am.

06:54.380 --> 06:55.540
I'll have some too.

06:55.540 --> 06:58.500
No way, you're still too young.

06:58.960 --> 07:00.420
That's not true.

07:00.420 --> 07:01.380
Hm?

07:01.670 --> 07:04.380
Even though you, Hazuki, and Tama say all say that,

07:05.000 --> 07:07.080
I've drank a whole cup of coffee.

07:10.000 --> 07:10.960
Really?

07:11.330 --> 07:12.880
What's with that reaction?

07:13.170 --> 07:16.580
I can hardly believe you can drink coffee now.

07:16.880 --> 07:18.540
I'm just a bit surprised.

07:21.670 --> 07:23.000
When did you drink coffee?

07:23.000 --> 07:24.540
I wanna hear this story.

07:24.830 --> 07:28.080
Hmm... I had some when I went out last week.

07:28.540 --> 07:31.630
The day Nagisa went out last week must have been...

07:34.750 --> 07:37.960
Nagisa was super, super conflicted about what to wear.

07:38.750 --> 07:42.040
Urgh. I can't do it right.

07:39.130 --> 07:43.250
That was the day she couldn't get her ponytail right,
and she redid it over and over again.

07:44.170 --> 07:46.170
Nagisa, do you want me to do that for you?

07:46.170 --> 07:47.580
What? Really?

07:48.170 --> 07:49.540
You would?

07:51.210 --> 07:54.170
Normally she would say, "I can do it myself!"

07:56.460 --> 07:59.920
That day Nagisa was acting
remarkably tractable, wasn't she?

08:07.710 --> 08:09.210
There, all done!

08:14.580 --> 08:15.750
Thank you!

08:15.750 --> 08:17.330
No problem!

08:20.250 --> 08:21.380
Hey, Akina.

08:21.380 --> 08:22.130
Hm?

08:23.250 --> 08:24.130
Um...

08:24.920 --> 08:25.580
Er...

08:26.380 --> 08:27.420
What's wrong?

08:30.540 --> 08:31.960
Does my outfit today

08:32.170 --> 08:33.420
look weird?

08:34.960 --> 08:36.710
Incidentally, that was the day

08:37.170 --> 08:43.040
I also asked myself, "Gosh! Who on earth
made Nagisa act so adorable?"

08:45.330 --> 08:46.580
Don't sweat it.

08:46.880 --> 08:49.750
My little sister is the cutest girl in the world.

08:51.580 --> 08:53.040
I get it now.

08:53.960 --> 08:56.920
There was that day and then coffee...

08:56.920 --> 08:59.880
As Nagisa grows up, there will be more
and more things I don't know about her.

08:59.880 --> 09:01.460
It makes me happy.

09:02.830 --> 09:06.040
Wah! But it also makes me feel lonely!

09:06.540 --> 09:07.460
Huh?

09:07.710 --> 09:12.250
Because when you were only thiiiiis big...

09:12.250 --> 09:13.380
Akina!

09:13.380 --> 09:16.170
You always followed me around.

09:16.420 --> 09:17.790
What are you talking about?

09:18.250 --> 09:23.500
You always used to imitate me
and listen to everything I told you.

09:24.580 --> 09:28.420
Are you upset that I drank coffee
without saying anything to you?

09:28.710 --> 09:30.210
I'm not upset.

09:30.920 --> 09:31.790
But...

09:33.580 --> 09:38.210
I was just thinking about how you're becoming more
and more of your own person without me even knowing.

09:39.380 --> 09:41.250
I may have not listened to you,

09:41.630 --> 09:43.790
but I'm probably still imitating you.

09:47.210 --> 09:51.920
I wanted to try drinking coffee because you drink coffee.

09:55.750 --> 09:57.670
I'm a little more like you now.

10:00.130 --> 10:01.830
And with that, I got your coffee!

10:01.830 --> 10:03.170
I'm gonna drink it in my room!

10:03.170 --> 10:04.960
Oh! Hey!

10:06.540 --> 10:08.380
She stole my coffee.

10:09.960 --> 10:11.750
I'll make some more.

10:12.330 --> 10:15.670
Even so, she says the most adorable things.

10:16.040 --> 10:19.040
I never thought I'd see the day
that Nagisa could tease me back.

10:19.790 --> 10:23.670
Aww. It's sad I'll have to give her away to someone else.

10:26.000 --> 10:30.000
<b>I didn't sweeten</b>

10:26.000 --> 10:30.000
<b>the coffee that</b>

10:26.000 --> 10:30.000
<b>Nagisa took.</b>

10:26.000 --> 10:30.000
<b>Will she be able</b>

10:26.000 --> 10:30.000
<b>to drink it?</b>

10:26.000 --> 10:30.000
<b>Fresh cup</b>

10:26.010 --> 10:30.000
<b>of coffee</b>

10:26.010 --> 10:30.000
<b>It's bitter...</b>

10:30.000 --> 10:35.000
<b>Haruka North High School</b>

10:35.000 --> 10:38.000
<b>Self-directed learning</b>

10:35.000 --> 10:38.000
<b>April 25th</b>

10:35.000 --> 10:38.000
<b>(Tues)</b>

10:35.000 --> 10:38.000
<b>Class duty</b>

10:35.000 --> 10:38.000
<b>Kudo / Mizuhara</b>

10:36.040 --> 10:37.630
Hello, everyone.

10:38.380 --> 10:39.960
I'm Junta Shiraishi.

10:41.000 --> 10:44.500
<b>Today's</b>

10:41.000 --> 10:44.500
<b>protagonist</b>

10:41.000 --> 10:46.540
<b>April</b>

10:41.000 --> 10:46.540
<b>25th</b>

10:41.380 --> 10:45.210
I know this it out of the blue, but today is my birthday.

10:46.710 --> 10:51.330
Speaking of which, when people born in
April are asked when their birthday is,

10:46.920 --> 10:54.540
<b>We're sending our viewers more close-ups of today's star!</b>

10:51.330 --> 10:53.000
often their birthday has already passed.

10:53.330 --> 10:56.540
Well, no one has ever asked me when my birthday is.

10:56.790 --> 11:01.040
Even though it's my birthday, I don't feel like
I'm in the starring role at all, just like any other day.

10:56.830 --> 11:01.540
<b>Main character meter</b>

11:01.750 --> 11:04.420
I wonder if I'll get cake at home.

11:05.000 --> 11:07.040
<b>Growl</b>

11:07.290 --> 11:09.290
Huh? Was that Shiraishi just now?

11:09.290 --> 11:10.880
That was super loud!

11:12.540 --> 11:17.040
<b>Main character meter</b>

11:12.880 --> 11:15.580
I didn't want to stand out because of this.

11:17.670 --> 11:19.920
Your stomach growling was
loud enough to wake the dead!

11:20.290 --> 11:21.540
Kubo-san.

11:21.790 --> 11:25.880
Everyone looked at you because
it was quiet in the classroom.

11:25.880 --> 11:27.540
It's rare for you to stand out like that.

11:27.790 --> 11:30.210
My stomach hurts just thinking about it.

11:30.920 --> 11:35.170
I've got something for you, today's oh-so-hungry star.

11:35.170 --> 11:36.170
Here you go.

11:39.920 --> 11:40.790
Thank you.

11:40.790 --> 11:41.830
My pleasure.

11:42.790 --> 11:44.880
It'd be embarrassing if your stomach growled again.

11:45.420 --> 11:46.420
That's true.

11:46.960 --> 11:49.790
But I'm starving, so I feel appreciative.

11:50.580 --> 11:54.580
<b>Happy birthday!</b>

11:58.880 --> 12:01.790
Happy birthday, Shiraishi-kun.

12:04.130 --> 12:06.960
Kubo-san, you knew it's my birthday?

12:07.210 --> 12:10.710
Oh, that's because I saw it on
your student ID card that one time.

12:11.080 --> 12:12.080
Back then...

12:12.630 --> 12:15.210
Shiraishi-kun, what's this?

12:12.920 --> 12:15.500
<b>Identification Card</b>

12:12.920 --> 12:15.500
<b>This document certifies that this person</b>

12:12.920 --> 12:15.500
<b>is a Haruka North High School student.</b>

12:12.920 --> 12:15.500
<b>Year 1 / Class 1</b>

12:12.920 --> 12:15.500
<b>Name:  Junta Shiraishi (16 years old)</b>

12:12.920 --> 12:15.500
<b>Date of birth: April 25th</b>

12:17.330 --> 12:20.330
<b>Happy birthday!</b>

12:24.710 --> 12:25.750
Aren't you going to eat it?

12:26.290 --> 12:27.330
Um.

12:28.080 --> 12:30.080
Does getting chocolate make you that happy?

12:30.750 --> 12:32.500
Then I'll give you another.

12:33.130 --> 12:33.830
Huh?

12:33.830 --> 12:35.540
Th-thanks.

12:38.080 --> 12:40.330
<b>Look in your desk</b>

12:54.500 --> 12:56.250
Can I open it?

12:56.750 --> 12:57.580
Go ahead.

13:00.000 --> 13:01.210
Isn't it cute?

13:01.670 --> 13:04.710
I thought it looked like you and bought it.

13:11.830 --> 13:15.000
I guess something like this is too cutesy for a boy?

13:15.460 --> 13:16.330
No.

13:20.420 --> 13:21.540
Thank you.

13:21.540 --> 13:22.880
I'll take good care of it.

13:26.250 --> 13:27.210
Okay!

13:27.210 --> 13:33.250
<b>April 25th</b>

13:27.210 --> 13:33.250
<b>(Tues)</b>

13:27.210 --> 13:33.250
<b>Class duty</b>

13:27.210 --> 13:33.250
<b>Kudo / Mizuhara</b>

13:27.420 --> 13:30.540
Um... When is your birthday?

13:30.540 --> 13:33.250
Me? It's August 2nd.

13:34.380 --> 13:36.750
Does that mean I should look forward
to a gift on my birthday?

13:40.040 --> 13:41.630
Keep your expectations low.

13:44.750 --> 13:45.670
All right.

13:46.960 --> 13:47.630
Oh!

13:47.630 --> 13:51.080
Well, you're hungry so eat up!

13:51.960 --> 13:54.250
Don't look so down.

13:57.250 --> 13:59.460
I'll get you a gift next year too.

14:00.960 --> 14:01.880
Got ya!

14:06.170 --> 14:07.290
Next year too?

14:07.540 --> 14:08.540
Of course!

14:10.420 --> 14:12.330
Huh? What? Are you choking?!

14:13.040 --> 14:15.710
No, I'm just feeling a little overwhelmed.

14:16.880 --> 14:21.250
No one's ever done anything for my birthday before,
and that alone makes me feel over the moon.

14:21.920 --> 14:23.130
Kubo-san.

14:24.380 --> 14:26.580
Thank you for remembering my birthday.

14:29.920 --> 14:31.540
You're welcome.

14:32.830 --> 14:34.330
Hey, Shiraishi-kun.

14:34.330 --> 14:35.630
Lift your head up.

14:36.210 --> 14:37.500
Shiraishi-kun!

14:38.080 --> 14:43.460
Kubo-san doesn't know how much
I struggled to not crack a smile.

14:53.630 --> 14:56.170
See you tomorrow, Shiraishi-kun!

14:56.630 --> 14:58.750
Yeah, see you tomorrow.

15:01.790 --> 15:03.420
Is Shiraishi here?

15:04.580 --> 15:06.420
Did he go home already?

15:06.420 --> 15:08.920
I forgot to return his handout.

15:09.960 --> 15:11.500
I'm behind you.

15:13.210 --> 15:16.290
I haven't seen Shiraishi recently. Is he absent?

15:16.290 --> 15:17.670
I heard he's here.

15:21.920 --> 15:23.960
I totally wanna get a good gacha pull!

15:24.170 --> 15:26.250
Why don't you find Shiraishi and then roll?

15:26.250 --> 15:27.040
Great idea!

15:42.420 --> 15:43.710
Did I imagine him?

15:44.380 --> 15:45.380
Quintuple take.

15:51.960 --> 15:52.960
Shiraishi-kun.

15:53.080 --> 15:54.000
Shiraishi-kun.

15:54.380 --> 15:55.710
It's Shiraishi-kun!

15:55.710 --> 15:57.000
Found ya, Shiraishi-kun!

15:57.000 --> 15:58.130
Shiraishi-kun!

15:58.250 --> 15:59.040
Shiraishi-kun.

15:59.040 --> 16:00.580
Good morning, Shiraishi-kun.

16:00.580 --> 16:02.170
I got a question for you, Shiraishi-kun.

16:02.170 --> 16:03.210
Shiraishi-kun.

16:03.210 --> 16:04.500
Shiraishi-kun?

16:05.630 --> 16:07.500
Why is Kubo-san

16:07.830 --> 16:09.920
the only one who can spot me?

16:21.920 --> 16:26.080
I first saw Shiraishi-kun in a photo
in my friend's yearbook.

16:26.540 --> 16:33.330
I thought it was weird that he got edited into
the photo even though he was already in it.

16:26.580 --> 16:35.790
<b>Junior High Graduation Commemoration Photo</b>

16:33.330 --> 16:35.670
I remember asking, "How did this happen to him?"

16:36.170 --> 16:39.540
Oh, it's because Shiraishi is invisible.

16:39.920 --> 16:43.670
We were in the same class for three years,
but I barely ever saw him.

16:43.670 --> 16:45.460
What? For real?

16:45.790 --> 16:48.210
Oh, we'll be in the same high school. Probably.

16:48.210 --> 16:50.380
I think the teacher said something about that.

16:50.750 --> 16:51.790
Huh...

16:52.250 --> 16:54.830
Gotcha. So his name is Shiraishi...

16:55.750 --> 16:58.920
I think that's when I first became interested in him.

16:59.580 --> 17:04.790
I casually wondered if I'd be able to spot him.

17:08.330 --> 17:10.670
Kubocchi, I'm so happy we're in the same class!

17:10.670 --> 17:12.170
Yeah, me too!

17:12.420 --> 17:13.210
Oh!

17:14.630 --> 17:18.130
That's the boy from Tama's yearbook, Shiraishi-kun!

17:19.000 --> 17:21.330
Tama said he's invisible,

17:21.330 --> 17:23.670
but he was surprisingly easy to spot.

17:24.920 --> 17:29.330
My first impression of him was,
well, that he's inexpressive.

17:30.290 --> 17:33.080
Hey, Tama. Shiraishi-kun's in our class.

17:33.080 --> 17:34.460
What, really?

17:34.830 --> 17:38.330
<b>Seating Chart</b>

17:34.830 --> 17:38.330
<b>Lectern</b>

17:34.840 --> 17:38.330
<b>Tamao Taira</b>

17:34.840 --> 17:38.330
<b>Hazuki Kudo</b>

17:34.840 --> 17:38.330
<b>Nagisa Kubo</b>

17:34.840 --> 17:38.330
<b>Junta Shiraishi</b>

17:35.420 --> 17:38.040
It's true! Shiraishi's name is on the chart!

17:38.670 --> 17:40.080
I'm surprised you noticed.

17:40.080 --> 17:42.540
Huh? Tama didn't notice?

17:43.500 --> 17:45.880
Well, he doesn't seem like
the type of guy who stands out.

17:46.040 --> 17:49.750
Maybe he tends to get overlooked?
That's what I thought, anyway.

17:53.130 --> 17:54.040
You were here?

17:54.420 --> 17:55.380
Yep.

17:56.750 --> 17:58.580
Shiraishi's absent?

17:59.170 --> 18:00.080
I'm here.

18:04.580 --> 18:06.790
Shiraishi, where are you?

18:07.380 --> 18:08.710
I'm right in front of you.

18:10.500 --> 18:12.630
How is he that invisible?

18:13.710 --> 18:16.330
Kubocchi's been laughing to herself a lot lately.

18:16.330 --> 18:17.290
Yeah.

18:17.880 --> 18:22.920
Shiraishi-kun's so invisible I never
see him talking to anyone else.

18:23.330 --> 18:25.790
I'm the only one they didn't get the handout from.

18:25.790 --> 18:29.960
No matter what happens, his expression barely changes.

18:30.960 --> 18:35.880
The more I watch him, I can't help
but become more curious about him.

18:36.580 --> 18:39.830
Does Shiraishi-kun ever laugh? Or get mad?

18:40.130 --> 18:43.080
I don't know because I've never
seen him talk to anyone else.

18:43.460 --> 18:45.290
Maybe I'll try talking to him sometime.

18:45.290 --> 18:46.670
But our paths never cross.

18:47.290 --> 18:48.460
Hey, did you hear?

18:48.830 --> 18:50.830
I heard we're changing seats today.

18:50.830 --> 18:52.250
Huh, changing seats?

18:52.250 --> 18:53.920
Yep! I can't wait!

18:53.920 --> 18:56.080
I hope our seats are close to each other.

18:56.080 --> 18:57.330
Yeah, me too!

18:58.080 --> 18:59.420
So, you two...

19:00.500 --> 19:03.290
Are there any boys you want to sit by?

19:03.290 --> 19:05.710
Geez Hazuki, you're so silly!

19:05.710 --> 19:07.250
Yeah, definitely not!

19:06.040 --> 19:07.380
That's the bell!

19:07.380 --> 19:10.250
Sit down! Today we're changing seats!

19:10.250 --> 19:11.380
Yes, sir!

19:18.750 --> 19:22.380
But if I do end up sitting near him...

19:22.380 --> 19:25.380
<b>Seating Chart</b>

19:22.380 --> 19:25.380
<b>Lectern</b>

19:25.500 --> 19:26.540
<b>Heart-pounding</b>

19:25.500 --> 19:26.540
<b>seat-change lottery</b>

19:25.540 --> 19:27.500
All right, you're up next, Kubo.

19:27.830 --> 19:28.880
Okay!

19:29.710 --> 19:32.210
That could be kinda fun, I thought.

19:33.750 --> 19:36.790
Two columns away from
the hallway side on the back row, huh?

19:38.630 --> 19:40.040
Kubocchi, where's your seat?

19:40.330 --> 19:41.130
Seat ten.

19:41.130 --> 19:42.880
What? That's so far away!

19:42.880 --> 19:45.080
That's a back-row seat. Lucky!

19:45.540 --> 19:46.460
Sure is!

19:46.830 --> 19:49.130
Well, I'm gonna move my stuff to my new desk.

19:49.130 --> 19:50.540
Aww!

19:52.040 --> 19:55.880
So I'm only admitting this in retrospect...

19:57.880 --> 19:58.830
Huh?

19:59.750 --> 20:05.130
But I was pretty excited to be
Shiraishi-kun's seat neighbor.

20:05.880 --> 20:09.130
I never thought I'd actually wind up
as his seat neighbor. I got lucky!

20:09.710 --> 20:12.580
Since we sit next to each other, it won't be weird
to strike up a conversation with him.

20:13.130 --> 20:14.830
Um, it's nice to meet you.

20:18.380 --> 20:19.000
Huh?

20:21.500 --> 20:24.540
Yeah, I'm talking to you, Shiraishi-kun.

20:25.670 --> 20:27.380
Huh? What's his deal?

20:28.170 --> 20:29.080
Um...

20:29.670 --> 20:30.830
Oh, um...

20:30.960 --> 20:32.460
N-nice to meet you too.

20:33.460 --> 20:35.670
Your voice cracked.

20:36.250 --> 20:37.130
Sorry.

20:37.130 --> 20:38.330
It's okay.

20:38.710 --> 20:39.750
Um...

20:39.750 --> 20:42.540
I don't stand out...

20:42.880 --> 20:45.920
I mean, people rarely see me.

20:45.920 --> 20:49.380
Well, I wasn't expecting you to talk to me.

20:49.670 --> 20:54.250
This is the first time someone has intentionally
talked to me since I started high school.

20:54.630 --> 20:55.750
Intentionally?

20:56.290 --> 20:58.630
It's just never happened to me before, so...

21:00.290 --> 21:01.630
Ah, okay.

21:01.880 --> 21:04.580
This is the first time I've seen Shiraishi-kun like this.

21:04.580 --> 21:06.290
Don't laugh, don't laugh.

21:06.880 --> 21:09.500
I know he doesn't really talk with anyone,

21:09.500 --> 21:11.170
but I'm really the first?

21:12.630 --> 21:14.130
She's kinda grinning.

21:14.670 --> 21:16.420
He's still shaking.

21:16.710 --> 21:17.670
Scary.

21:18.170 --> 21:22.710
When I talked to him, I realized
he's easier to read than I thought he'd be.

21:23.130 --> 21:26.170
But I still don't know what he's thinking.

21:26.500 --> 21:32.000
Knowing I'm the only one in our class who's seen
this aspect of Shiraishi-kun makes me a little happy

21:33.040 --> 21:35.580
I suppose you could call it a superiority complex.

21:37.960 --> 21:40.170
I'll try telling him good morning tomorrow.

21:40.580 --> 21:42.630
I wonder what facial expression he'll make?

21:58.040 --> 22:00.380
Shiraishi-kun, see you tomorrow.

22:03.920 --> 22:08.710
I don't think I'll be able to take my eyes off
Shiraishi-kun for a while.

22:10.330 --> 22:13.130
Jikan yo tomare
Please, just for a moment<b></b>

22:13.130 --> 22:17.170
Sukoshi dake
Let the time freeze<b></b>

22:19.460 --> 22:22.750
Hajimari wa itsu datta?
When did it start?<b></b>

22:22.750 --> 22:26.420
Mou oboetenai kedo
I cannot remember<b></b>

22:27.250 --> 22:31.000
Sore mo ii ka tte sa
Who actually cares?<b></b>

22:31.000 --> 22:33.750
Taai mo nai koto
"It doesn't matter"<b></b>

22:34.330 --> 22:37.580
Itsudatte ki ga tsukeba
Laughing or shedding tears<b></b>

22:37.580 --> 22:41.500
Waratte naitari shite
Whenever we realized<b></b>

22:41.960 --> 22:47.460
Tamani iji hattari mo shitari ne
Or too persistent to take in sometime<b></b>

22:48.960 --> 22:58.710
Shingou ga kawareba seeno de susumu ikisaki (konomama)
Ready? And go as the traffic light changes (As we are)<b></b>

22:58.710 --> 23:02.670
Iwanakutemo (dokomademo)
No words needed (as far as we can be)<b></b>

23:02.830 --> 23:05.790
Ikeru yo ne kitto
we can surely make it<b></b>

23:05.790 --> 23:09.460
Dramatic janakutemo
Even if it wasn't dramatic<b></b>

23:09.630 --> 23:13.290
Taikutsu da to nagetemo
Even if it was boring and I was moaning<b></b>

23:13.580 --> 23:18.540
Itsuka futo omoidasu
I'll remember this day<b></b>

23:19.000 --> 23:20.170
Kyou o
When? I don't know<b></b>

23:20.540 --> 23:24.250
Romantic na kotoba mo
I don't need no romantic words<b></b>

23:24.420 --> 23:27.830
Nakute ii yo dakara
I just want one thing<b></b>

23:27.920 --> 23:30.580
Jikan yo tomare
Let the time freeze<b></b>

23:30.580 --> 23:34.500
Sukoshi dake
Just for a moment...<b></b>

23:35.170 --> 23:37.460
Todoku kana
Will this feeling reach you?<b></b>
